      "text": "VT-7\nEAGLES\nCDR Thomas L. Kellner NAS MERIDIAN, MISSISSIPPI CDR Adam J. Fisel\nCommanding Officer Executive Officer\nSaturday, 28-Nov-2026\nSUNRISE: 06:38 MOONRISE: 21:22 ILLUM: 82% JULIAN DATE: 6332\nSUNSET: 16:49 MOONSET: 10:47\nTOTAL FLY EVENTS: 0 TOTAL FLY HRS: 0.0 SYL FLY EVENTS: 0 SYL FLY HRS: 0.0\nTOTAL SIM EVENTS: 0 TOTAL SIM HRS: 0.0 SYL SIM EVENTS: 0 SYL SIM HRS: 0.0\nQuestions:\nEP Question: SUCCESSFUL AIRSTART.\nTHE MAJOR DIFFERENCE BETWEEN ENGINE MALFUNCTIONS WHILE IN NORMAL FUEL CONTROL AND ENGINE MALFUNCTIONS\nWHILE IN MANUAL FUEL CONTROL IS THAT WHEN IN MANUAL FUEL CONTROL, A. YOU NEED NOT PAY ATTENTION TO ENGINE\nNATOPS:\nINDICATORS. B. THROTTLE MOVEMENTS MUST BE MADE JUDICIOUSLY. C. ENGINE MALFUNCTION INDICATIONS OCCUR AT A\nFASTER RATE. D. REACTION TIME TO MALFUNCTIONS IS INCREASED.\nSOP: WHAT ARE THE SINGLE AIRCRAFT NORDO PROCEDURES?\nDUTY/WATCH ASSIGNED SIGN IN SIGN OUT\nODO (ON CALL) NORTON, OWEN T, 1stLt 0000 2359\nDUTY DRIVER MIDTHUN, NOAH J, LTJG 0000 2359\nIWO KANAYA, EMILO, ENS 0600 1800\nIWO GIBBS, REESE, ENS 1800 0600\nCOMMENTS:\nNMM: CLOSED\nNJW: CLOSED\nR-4404: CLOSED\nAREA 1/2/3/4: CLOSED\nMERIDIAN 2 MOA: CLOSED\nAF USING BHAM MOA: NONE\nAF USING SEARAY: NONE\nAF USING PINE HILLS/CAMDEN RIDGE: NONE\nVT-7 FCLP: NMM: NONE; NJW: NONE\nVT-9 FCLP: NMM: NONE; NJW: NONE\nRESERVISTS ON ACTIVE DUTY: NONE\nRESERVISTS DRILLING: NONE\n***MISSION COMMANDERS ASSIGNED IAW SOP***\nR/S: 0; W/U: 0; FITU: 0\nADVANCING X\u2019s: 0\nSIT: 63\nUPCOMING OPS:\n2 DEC: ROBD / IGS\n11 DEC: HOLIDAY PARTY\n12 DEC: CHILDREN\u2019S HOLIDAY PARTY\n22 JAN: WINGING"
